kslash ddot\{\textbackslash nu\}\}\$ is a stellar damping time-scale, and \$T\_\{\textbackslash rm obs\}\$ is the total observing time. When the inequality in the above condition is reversed, \$n\$ is dominated by the secular braking torque, and timing measurements return \$n\textbackslash sim 3\$, if the secular braking torque is electromagnetic. The variance \$\textbackslash langle n\textasciicircum 2 \textbackslash rangle\$ is greater, when the stochastic process driving spin fluctuations differs from the red noise model (e.g. power-law spectral density) assumed in the timing solution.},
